vanessa bryant continues her case in  court seeking justice for her late  husband kobe bryant and daughter gianna  who were killed in a 2020 helicopter  crash  on friday vanessa emotionally testified  detailing her life and trauma since the  accident  we love and miss you boo boo and gigi  according to cnn while vanessa was on  the witness stand she claimed she  experiences panic attacks and anxiety  over possibly seeing photos from the  accident the outlet reports that vanessa  recalled the day she got the  heartbreaking news  quote i bolted out of the house and i  ran to the side of the house so the  girls couldn't see me i wanted to run  down the block and just scream i can't  escape my body i can't escape what i  feel  she's suing the la sheriffs and fire  department over photos taken at the  tragic scene that were shared for  personal use  and on the stand vanessa recalled her  interaction with authorities  after sheriff alex villanueva informed  her that kobe and gigi died vanessa said  he asked her if there was anything he  could do her response quote if you can't  bring my babies back then please secure  the area i'm concerned about paparazzi  vanessa claims sheriff villanueva  assured her that he would honor her  request and informed her that he secured  a temporary flight restriction over the  area  e.t has reached out to vanessa's legal  team for comment  in a dramatic opening statement her  attorney claimed law enforcement  exploited the accident by taking and  sharing pictures of kobe and gianna as  souvenirs  former fire captain brian jordan took  the stand to testify on monday but  walked off the witness stand three times  citing stress from working the crash as  his reason for repeatedly excusing  himself  attorney also told jurors the photos  were virtual gossip and played security  video of an off-duty sheriff's deputy  showing them to a bartender to support  that claim  sheriff's deputy joey cruz is the  officer in question he's accused of  sharing photos at the scene cruz  admitted he took it too far and said  it's something i shouldn't have done  meanwhile kobe's widow is receiving an  outpour of love from family and friends  including the late nba star's former  teammate shaquille o'neal who expressed  to e.t his empathy for vanessa  i couldn't imagine what she's going  through  we live in a world where  especially when it hits the internet  people don't care but  those aren't pictures that i would ever  ever want to see so  you know she's doing a great thing for  you know how many people as possible  you
 

